# Engineering Playbook

A personal collection of software engineering learnings, system design notes, architecture tradeoffs, implementation patterns, and lessons gathered from real-world development and engineering discussions.

## Purpose

This repository is not a tutorial series or a collection of copied articles.

The goal is to document:

* System design concepts
* Architecture decisions and tradeoffs
* Backend engineering patterns
* Distributed systems learnings
* Scaling strategies
* Interview and career insights
* Lessons learned from real engineering problems

Over time, this becomes a searchable engineering knowledge base.

---

## Repository Structure

```text
engineering-playbook/
├── system-design/
├── backend/
├── distributed-systems/
├── architecture/
├── databases/
├── cloud/
├── career/
└── README.md
```

---

## Note Format

Most notes follow a simple structure:

```text
Problem

Possible Solutions

Tradeoffs

Decision

Key Learnings
```

The focus is understanding *why* a solution works and *when* it should be used rather than memorizing implementation details.

